\section*{Question 1}
\begin{itemize}
\item[] Let \(R\) be the shaded region bounded by the graph of \(y=\ln x\) and the line \(y=x-2\), as shown above.
\item[(a)] Find the area of \(R\).
\item[(b)] Find the volume of the solid generated when \(R\) is rotated about the horizontal line \(y=-3\).
(c) Write, but do not evaluate, an integral expression that can be used to find the volume of the solid generated when \(R\) is rotated about the \(y\)-axis.
![](https://cdn.mathpix.com/cropped/418884ee-0888-40de-8286-463f5960fd7d-1.jpg?height=556&width=475&top_left_y=333&top_left_x=1472)
\end{itemize}
\(\ln (x)=x-2\) when \(x=0.15859\) and 3.14619.
Let \(S=0.15859\) and \(T=3.14619\)
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] Area of \(R=\int_{S}^{T}(\ln (x)-(x-2)) d x=1.949\)
\item[(b)]
\[
\begin{aligned}
\text { Volume } & =\pi \int_{S}^{T}\left((\ln (x)+3)^{2}-(x-2+3)^{2}\right) d x \\
& =34.198 \text { or } 34.199
\end{aligned}
\]
\item[(c)] Volume \(=\pi \int_{S-2}^{T-2}\left((y+2)^{2}-\left(e^{y}\right)^{2}\right) d y\)
\end{itemize}
